# Database Patterns

## Prisma Client

```typescript
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";
```

## Types

Use Prisma-generated types:

```typescript
import { User, Product, Order } from "@/lib/generated/prisma";
```

## Key Models

| Model | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `User` | Auth & user data (email, password, role: CUSTOMER/ADMIN) |
| `Product` | E-commerce catalog |
| `Cart` / `CartItem` | Shopping cart |
| `Order` | Order management with status |
| `Address` | User and order addresses |
| `Flag` | CTF flags (slug, category, difficulty) |
| `Hint` | 3 progressive hints per flag (levels 1-3) |
| `RevealedHint` | Tracks which hints a player has unlocked |
| `FoundFlag` | Tracks which flags a player has captured |
| `Review` | Product reviews |
| `SupportAccessToken` | Support access tokens |

## Commands

```bash
npm run db:generate   # Generate Prisma Client
npm run db:push       # Push schema changes
npm run db:migrate    # Run migrations
npm run db:studio     # Open Prisma Studio
npm run db:seed       # Seed with initial data and flags
```

## Seeding Flags

Flags and hints live in `prisma/flags.ts`, the single source of truth for the CTF curriculum. `prisma/seed.ts` imports them and upserts them by slug — don't add flags to `seed.ts` directly.

```typescript
// prisma/flags.ts
export const flags: ChallengeFlag[] = [
  // ...
  {
    flag: "OSS{example_flag}",
    slug: "vulnerability-slug",
    markdownFile: "vulnerability-slug.md",
    walkthroughSlug: "vulnerability-writeup",
    category: "INJECTION",
    difficulty: "MEDIUM",
  },
];

export const flagHints: Record<string, string[]> = {
  // ...
  "vulnerability-slug": ["Vague nudge.", "Clearer direction.", "Near-solution."],
};
```

`tests/unit/challenge-parity.test.ts` validates every entry against the rest of the repo. Run `npm run test:unit` after editing this file. See `CONTRIBUTING.md` ("Adding a challenge") for the full flow.

Other seed data (users, products, orders, coupons, gift cards) stays in `prisma/seed.ts`.
